task: free-bind-node-count (measurement first: the floor of a bind without the effect injection)
agent: okay-42
started: 2026-09-06
branch: feature/free-bind-node-count

why: native-interpreter-allocation counted ~six objects / 135 B per
  `async(i).flatMap(f)` and showed the count IS the Native cost. Before
  any change to Free's ADT, the upper bound of what removing the
  injection could buy: a `pureChain` lane (`okay.pure(i).flatMap(f)`:
  Pure + Bind + closure, no Inject/Run/thunk) beside `bindChain`, on
  Native and under JMH -prof gc. If pureChain on Native is near
  bindChain, the effect wrapper is not the cost and the entry closes as
  "no"; if it is near half, the fused-node question is worth a design
  entry with a number on it. BenchCross + PerElementStepBenchmark only.
